    <string name="compat_cur_off">Status: not enabled</string>
    <string name="compat_explain">Some hardened apps (e.g. the digital RMB app) crash right after launch on rooted devices: their self-check deliberately crashes when it sees SELinux Enforcing together with root.\n\nThis fix bind-mounts a shadow over /sys/fs/selinux/enforce that reads 0, so the protection treats the environment as non-Enforcing and lets the app run.\n\n· The real SELinux state and access control are completely unchanged\n· Takes effect immediately, no reboot needed\n· Must be re-enabled after a reboot / soft reboot\n· While mounted, tools like getenforce wrongly show Permissive (they read the shadow)\n· Disabling simply unmounts it and fully restores the original</string>
